[Music]  if you're wondering how new technology  can make your life easier we've got some  answers for you this morning from a  countertop dishwasher to a robot that  can give you massages okay okay  we're getting a look at some of this  year's latest gadgets the consumer  technology association's annual  conference called ces kicks off today  preparations have been made in las vegas  where the event will be in person and  virtual this year as covet cases soared  big names like google microsoft amazon  and gm pulled out from in-person  portions cnet's editor-at-large brian  cooley joins us right now good morning  brian how are you doing  good morning nate i'm doing fine i am  not in las vegas i'm one of those many  uh people who decided to cover the show  but not go to the show  it's all right you got the technology  that will get you covered um so talk to  me about these monitors that i'm hearing  about that could change the way you work  at home and watch tv yeah look at these  they're very enveloping the idea here  across the tv industry these are being  showed by lg is that you'll have a  monitor that is so large you look at  that and so curved under and above you  that it's almost like a place more than  just a device you look down you see the  road you look up you see the trees and  of course you look forward and you have  a peloton-like view this is part of the  pelotonization of so many products  brian that is so cool looking also looks  very big let's talk about the health  aspect i swear by the apple watch i wear  it every day it gives me so much  information i know people wear fitbits  but i'm hearing you have something there  called a ring that can also monitor your  health how does that work  yeah so there are there was a ring out a  couple of years ago we talked about uh  gale that was a little on the pricey  side called ura this is a new one from a  company called movano uh not yet on the  market it's promised to be a lot less  expensive and yet still monitor all of  those indications you see on the screen  activity respiration heart rate or  problems with your heart rhythm and then  in the future potentially blood pressure  and blood glucose that remains kind of a  holy grail still in the industry the  idea here is unlike people like you gail  who adopted smart watches early a lot of  people have got no health wearable on  them at all and we've got to get at  least one health wearable on everybody  in the next 10 years because it's  ridiculous that we only get our signals  checked once a year at the doctor  i know i fell recently and the watch  started talking to me saying you know  seems like you fell are you okay and i  was shocked i go yes i'm fine don't call  anybody don't call anybody but how do  you make sure that you're  how do you make sure that your  health information is secure  the two main things here first of all  many of these devices are covered by  hipaa the federal law that secures your  health data if they connect to a doctor  or connect to your health records which  many of these do now that's not  considered uncommon anymore or at the  very least when you set it up make sure  you take your time the first time and  uncheck any boxes about data sharing  that you're not comfortable with a lot  of folks blow through that  all right brian we are also hearing  about what is being described as a  human-like robot i think we'll judge  that when we see it what can you tell us  about this thing  yes sit down for this one tony it's a  real seriously human-looking robot this  is called a mika from a company called  engineered arts uk company look at that  so what they're saying is look we've  made a lot of progress in a.i the  intelligence that powers various robots  that we've talked about over the years  but where's the progress in the physical  sort of nuance of them and that's what  they're doing here saying the physical  nuance needs to be as good as the  intelligence and that we're building  into these otherwise the whole sort of  idea of it being convincing starts to  fall apart this is an extremely  realistic looking device to be in front  of now it's not going to be coming to  markets or homes anytime soon but you  can see where we're going  yeah brian what does it do i don't know  what it does well i want to get in on  one particular robot that i know what it  does it doesn't look like a human being  it's a massage robot we showed some  video of it just at the top of the  segment there it is  uh what do we know about that we know  what it does right this gives you a  massage this is either the best or the  worst thing in the world of massage  depending on how you feel about a human  massage therapist some people say that's  the best thing about it i've got this  person who's working out all these nuts  and kinks others say i don't want to be  mostly disrobed in front of anybody i  don't know so depending on where you  fall on the massage  experience spectrum this could be great  or it could make absolutely no sense to  you and it's from a company that builds  massage robots  when it comes to robots i feel like i've  seen this in a movie before um and it  didn't turn out good but brian cooley  thank you so much um we appreciate you  joining us

